 ],
 "notes": "Photos 00, sheet1 and sheet2 show the garden side: two storeys of white plaster boxes with thin flat roofs, a pale stone-clad vertical core between the main block and a wing with a cantilevered roof slab, large black-framed glazing on both floors, a planter ledge with hanging vines on the upper floor, a dark pool in a grey paver terrace with daybeds and palms, a lawn, and a bare hillside rising behind. Interiors (white marble, steel kitchen, living room) are not modelled. Renders: round 1 the hill was a tall dark soil wall and the pool was paved over; round 2 hill lowered to a dry-grass slope with a low concrete retaining wall, pool basin cut so the water shows, glass recessed behind dark interiors. Still off: the pool should read darker teal, vines are drawn only as a planter ledge, the hill is a plain ramp, the roof slabs are heavier than the photos' thin edges. Guessed: all dimensions, the L plan and which way the wing runs, the hill's height and slope, lawn size, tree positions. Placed only at the city of Lima. Round 3: pool water set to dark slate-teal, roof slabs thinned to 0.25-0.3 m, vines hung from the planter ledge."
